/E (When optimizing for cycle times, the size of the intake are critical. Our original REV-based design could only collect one artifact at a time, making it highly inefficient. The first iteration of our goBILDA-based design improved capacity to two artifacts but proved awkward in practice. In the final iteration, we implemented an overhang intake, significantly increasing efficiency by allowing the robot to collect multiple artifacts at once. This design widened the margin of error for drivers, resulting in faster and consistent cycle times.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [15]
>>
