/Title (Why PedroPathing over Roadrunner Through testing, we found PedroPathing was more precise at higher accelerations and better at correcting unexpected disturbances mid-path, which directly improves autonomous consistency.)
/Dest [20 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1523 0 R
/Prev 1605 0 R
/Next 1655 0 R
>>
endobj
1655 0 obj
<<
/Title (The Math Behind Reactive Vector Followers Pedro Pathing combines an attractive force pulling the robot toward the goal with repulsive forces avoiding obstacles. Recalculating the ideal movement vector every loop cycle. Overall pedropathing has so many good features its hard not to pick it.)
/Dest [20 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1523 0 R
/Prev 1654 0 R
/Next 1606 0 R
>>
endobj
1656 0 obj
<<
/Title (Our autonomous routine uses a 4-state Finite State Machine. The robot begins IDLE, then skips using the Limelight 3A to ALIGN to the target since the robot can just go to a preset point, SPINs UP the shooter to the calculated RPM, then LAUNCHes. This structure ensures each action only begins when the previous is complete, improving reliability.)
/Dest [20 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1606 0 R
/Next 1657 0 R
>>
endobj
1657 0 obj
<<
/Title (4 Autonomous Strategy We developed four autonomous routines for different starting positions on the field, allowing our robot to adapt based on alliance strategy and partner positioning. These routines are split between starting near the GOAL and starting in the back LAUNCH ZONE, each optimized for efficient pathing, fast cycling, and consistent scoring. By using smooth trajectories and coordinated intake/shooting sequences, each autonomous has the potential to score up to 12 ARTIFACTS while minimizing downtime and maximizing reliability.)
/Dest [20 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1606 0 R
/Prev 1656 0 R
>>
endobj
